,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Rule 6c-11 website disclosures (public, free, as of 2026-11-06)**\n\n**Portfolio holdings (daily):** Before the primary exchange opens each business day, post the full holdings used for that day's NAV. Each holding needs a ticker, CUSIP or other identifier, description, quantity, and percentage weight.\n\n**Daily data (prior business day):** NAV, market price (closing price or NBBO midpoint), and the premium/discount.\n\n**History:** A table or chart of daily premiums/discounts covering the most recent calendar year and the calendar quarters completed since then. Funds younger than that show their full life.\n\n**Spread:** The median bid-ask spread over the most recent 30 days.\n\n**Sustained deviation:** If the premium/discount exceeds 2% for more than seven consecutive trading days, post that fact and the factors believed to have materially contributed. This is due the next trading day and must stay posted at least one year.\n\n**Baskets:** Daily publication is not required. ETFs need basket policies and procedures and must keep records of AP baskets, including custom-basket documentation, for five years. Holdings and baskets can differ.","ttft_ms":8674,"type":"result","duration_ms":12419,"uuid":"0cd58407-d46e-4ec5-92ac-1ccc1e845ba9","ttft_stream_ms":1526,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":1526,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
